fastdedup (0.1.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Modernize: Go 1.26 baseline, CI, e2e suite, wave-budget and dedup-count fixes, packaging refresh
  * Fix wave mode silently skipping size groups that exceed --mem-budget: such groups are now processed individually via a per-size scan
  * Fix dedup-count inflation when a new duplicate is walked before an already-deduped family: counts are now walk-order-independent and new duplicates always join the existing reflink family
  * Require Go 1.26 or newer and rename the module to github.com/phntom/fastdedup; restructure main into main.go + run.go
  * Add GitHub Actions CI (ci.yml) and a black-box end-to-end test suite
  * Packaging refresh: golang-1.26-go (>= 1.26~) in debian/control, bundled Go 1.26.8 toolchain for the EOL PPA series (oracular, plucky, questing)

